    "body": "A couple things 1) there seems to be some conflicts on this branch, perhaps your fork is a few PRs behind? 2) I think a big question is whether to implement the reordering as a method on FermionOperator or an external function. In general, we try very hard to keep these methods as external functions. One of the reasons is because we ultimately intend to implement the core data structures in C++ (one day) and it will be much easier to make changes like this if we keep the core classes lean. I am in favor of having this be an external function rather than a method. What do others think?\r\n\r\nAlso, should we perhaps have this reordering be general to SymbolicOperator rather than FermionOperator?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
